Find the volume of each rectangular prism. Do they have the same volume?

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
% Closed rectangular prisms: front, rear, left, right, top and bottom faces.
% View from the front, above and right; the rear-bottom-left vertex is obscured.
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (3,0); \coordinate (C) at (3,2); \coordinate (D) at (0,2);
\coordinate (E) at (0.8,0.7); \coordinate (F) at (3.8,0.7); \coordinate (G) at (3.8,2.7); \coordinate (H) at (0.8,2.7);
\draw[black] (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle (B)--(F)--(G)--(C) (D)--(H)--(G);
\draw[black,dashed] (A)--(E)--(F) (E)--(H);
\path (1.5,-0.45) node {8 cm} (3.65,0.15) node[right] {3 cm} (-0.15,1) node[left] {2 cm} (1.9,3.15) node {Prism A};
\begin{scope}[xshift=62mm]
\coordinate (J) at (0,0); \coordinate (K) at (2,0); \coordinate (L) at (2,2); \coordinate (M) at (0,2);
\coordinate (N) at (1,1); \coordinate (O) at (3,1); \coordinate (P) at (3,3); \coordinate (Q) at (1,3);
\draw[black] (J)--(K)--(L)--(M)--cycle (K)--(O)--(P)--(L) (M)--(Q)--(P);
\draw[black,dashed] (J)--(N)--(O) (N)--(Q);
\path (1,-0.45) node {4 cm} (2.65,0.3) node[right] {3 cm} (-0.15,1) node[left] {4 cm} (1.5,3.45) node {Prism B};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

Diagrams are not to scale.
